<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Hardened-runtime entitlements for the frozen `tan` executable (tan-cli#1506).
  Kept to the one the CPython runtime needs: ctypes/libffi (used by truststore
  to reach the macOS Security framework) allocates executable closure pages,
  which hardened runtime blocks without allow-unsigned-executable-memory.
  disable-library-validation is deliberately NOT granted: every bundled dylib
  is signed by macos_sign.sh with the SAME identity, so library validation
  passes. If a signed freeze fails to start, test_packaged_binary.py (run right
  after the freeze) fails the leg; add an entitlement only on that evidence.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
